name issue_446_cwnd_after_outage
describe video-only call, 4 s outage at 15 s on both paths, seed 3: congestion-window pushback holds through the retransmissions after link-up, as libwebrtc (#446)
# issue_430_video_only_outage_4s on seed 3. After link-up the sender retransmits what the receiver NACKs
# (about 150 RTX packets in 0.8 s, the same on both stacks). libwebrtc keeps pushing back the encoder
# (every other frame dropped, encoder target half the allocation) until the data in flight falls under
# 10 % of the congestion window: GoogCcNetworkController::OnTransportPacketsFeedback runs the pushback
# before UpdateCongestionWindowSize (goog_cc_network_control.cc:421-541). Before #446 this library resized the
# window first, so the first feedback after link-up ended the pushback and the encoder sent the full target
# into the queue the retransmissions held.
#   cc.queue_p95_ms, seed 3: main before the fix 92.1, after 51.6, libwebrtc 65 (compare-webrtc @ a78522c).
#   10 seeds: before 67.1, after 53.1, libwebrtc 52.7 (worst seed 71).
seed 3
duration 40s
audio off
at 0s capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
at 15s down
at 19s up
reverse at 0s delay=30ms
reverse at 15s down
reverse at 19s up
# PR for #518 (harness: timers at their due microsecond, the sides more alike; program.md 0.2's exception, up to
# libwebrtc's worst seed): was < 70. Ours 71.1 on seed 3 (seeds 1-10 mean 56.6, main 54.1); libwebrtc 47.6 on seed 3,
# seeds 1-10 mean 64.5, worst 121.1.
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 75
expect video.pause_total_ms < 6900
expect video.render_fps > 22.7
